Why: On macOS keys for an Open/Save panel go to the panel service process that draws it, so Go to Folder, Escape, arrows and Return work on a background panel, and its Go to Folder sheet counts as the panel's key window; the front guard watches the window order from the start of each action with its own restore cap, so a sheet the panel orders in is put back under the user's window within a poll (#675).

